          <p class="body">Three steps, one directory.</p>
          <ol class="doclist doclist--num">
            <li><strong>Install</strong>
              <span>The command above adds the <span class="mono">sagan-wire</span>
                installer to your Claude Code setup.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Wire your project</strong>
              <span>Say &ldquo;wire this project to sagan.&rdquo; It probes your
                repo, captures your real test/build commands, and installs a
                self-contained <span class="mono">.sagan/</span> folder. One
                directory in; delete it to walk away.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Run your first ticket</strong>
              <span>Copy the <a href="https://github.com/thewhatmatters/sagan/blob/main/tickets/T-000-example.md">example ticket</a>, write what &ldquo;done&rdquo; means,
                then say <span class="mono">/sagan-start</span> to bring your
                tickets into the repo and refuse any that don&rsquo;t say what
                done means &mdash; and <span class="mono">/sagan-run</span> to
                drive the circuit: build, critique, verify, and a promote
                decision that stays yours. Tickets can live as files in your
                repo or in Linear.</span></li>
          </ol>
        </div>

